# Table chrome

Use shared table chrome from `src/lib/table-styles.ts` (CSS in `globals.css`). Do not invent one-off table frames or header backgrounds.

## Variants

| Variant | Classes | When |
|---|---|---|
| **Shell** | `TABLE_SHELL` | Outer wrapper around **div** grids (Month calendar) |
| **Frame** | `TABLE_FRAME` | Border on the **`<table>`** itself (Week plan) — avoids wrapper/cell gaps |
| **Primary header** | `TABLE_HEADER`, `TABLE_HEADER_CELL*`, `TABLE_HEADER_VLINE` | Week plan, Month calendar, Season planner |
| **Sub header** | `TABLE_HEADER_SUB` | Secondary strip under a primary header |
| **Muted header** | `TABLE_HEADER_MUTED` | Sparse list tables (race lists, results, personal bests) |

## Rules

- Table frames are **square** (`rounded-none`) — never rounded corners on table chrome.
- Week plan tables use `TABLE_FRAME` on `<table>`, not a bordered wrapper around the table.
- Do not put `border-r` on the last day column — the frame/shell is the outer edge.
- Prefer importing constants from `@/lib/table-styles` over duplicating border strings.
- Add new variants only in `globals.css` + `table-styles.ts`.
